WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.730
The Terminator has spawned an entire entertainment
franchise, one that includes films, TV series,

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.100
and now-defunct amusement park attractions.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.840
But, as with any franchise out there, not
all installments are created equal.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.600
Here's how the films and shows stack up, from
worst to best.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:24.180
The Terminator franchise had already put out
two immensely successful releases by 2003,

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.960
when Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines came
out.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.960
It marked the first film without any involvement
from series creator James Cameron.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.080
It shows.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.520
Rise of the Machines is all style and zero
substance, one of those films that throws

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.720
everything that worked from its predecessors
at the wall and winds up making a giant mess

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.220
with it.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.560
The chases are bigger, but definitely not
better.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.560
Somehow, more explosions happen than in either
previous movie, but they don't seem to be

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.719
there for any reason other than someone decided
it was a Terminator movie, and Terminator

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.220
movies need explosions.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:02.140
Rise of the Machines is basically the same
movie as Judgment Day, only with a female

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.700
Terminator chasing after John Connor while
Arnold Schwarzenegger's T-800 attempts to

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:07.440
protect him.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:13.560
Just prior to the release of 2009's Terminator
Salvation, Machinima released this tie-in

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.180
web series.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:20.470
Terminator Salvation: The Machinima Series
takes place in 2016, two years prior to the

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:25.540
events of Salvation the movie, and it centers
on Blair Williams as she sets out on a mission

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:30.100
to hunt down "the Ghost," a hacker who’s
interfering with Resistance communications.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.979
If you can get past the mediocre effects,
The Machinima Series manages to be a pretty

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.299
entertaining series.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.659
It doesn't add anything or take away from
the franchise, the story doesn't affect the

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.680
greater Skynet threat in the long run, but
it gets points for creativity.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:49.640
And out of all the Terminator films, the fact
that Salvation managed to be the one to get

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.280
its own offshoot web series as a marketing
ploy is pretty daring.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:59.060
Following up Rise of the Machines, Terminator
Salvation tells the bleak, post-Judgment Day

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.320
story of the Resistance and its fighters.

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:06.159
There were hopes that the film would reinvigorate
the franchise, and for a time, it seemed as

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:06.860
though it would.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:12.740
Jonathan Nolan, the award-winning writer behind
The Dark Knight, Interstellar, and HBO's Westworld,

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:16.580
had started work on the script but pulled
out due to another commitment.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.320
Then there was a writers’ strike.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.880
Salvation just couldn't seem to catch a break.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:27.220
In 2018, star Christian Bale appeared on MTV's
Happy Sad Confused podcast and touched on

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:27.720
his regrets.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.080
Bale said:

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.830
"I said no three times.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:36.780
And it's a great thorn in my side, because
I wish we could have reinvigorated that.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.200
And unfortunately, during production, you
could tell that wasn't happening.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.800
But it's a great shame."

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:47.480
At least Salvation isn't another retelling
of the first three films.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.950
In this one, John Connor is a fully-fledged
resistance leader, Kyle Reese is a young,

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:57.300
pre-time traveling Sarah Connor-romancer,
and the main cyborg doesn't even know he's

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:57.960
a machine.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.280
"Who built you?"

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.239
"My name is Marcus Wright."

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.480
"You think you're human?"

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.280
"I am human."

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.540
Terminator Genisys

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:12.659
Terminator Genisys, the 2015 franchise reboot,
was supposed to be the film that really would

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.520
bring fans back to the fold.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.080
Even James Cameron told Yahoo!

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:21.580
Movies that he felt as though Genisys worked
as the true third installment in the Terminator

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:22.260
franchise.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:27.810
With a story centered on fractured timelines
and unexpected villains, Genisys really is

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.280
the best film to come out since Terminator
2.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:35.400
But saying that it's better than the two films
before it isn't really saying much at all.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.780
The most successful thing about Genisys is
the way it treats its source material.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.480
Using a combination of fancy CGI work and
reenactments with body doubles who look just

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.390
enough like the '84 actors to get by, Genisys
pays a great deal of fan service to those

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.760
who loved the original.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.520
Where it fails is in trying to weave in new
material.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:04:00.620
Nearly everything that takes place in the
new 2017 timeline is confusing, but seeing

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.840
a 1984 Sarah Connor kick ass kind of makes
up for it.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:09.480
For two seasons, The Sarah Connor Chronicles
gave fans hope that the franchise could, in

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.060
fact, get back on track.

00:04:11.689 --> 00:04:16.340
Taking place after the events of Terminator
2, the series sees Sarah and a teenage John

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:20.940
Connor running from yet another Terminator,
with the help of a cyborg named Cameron.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:21.820
Get it?

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.060
Cameron?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:29.750
The Sarah Connor Chronicles jumps in time
from 1997 to 2007, effectively erasing Rise

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.640
of the Machines.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:35.600
Sarah and John are able to exist in a timeline
more in line with Terminator 2.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:39.160
Sarah is still alive and a key figure in the
Resistance.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:43.800
Star Lena Headey manages to pick up where
Linda Hamilton left off in a way that feels

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.660
more like an homage to the original character
than someone trying to replace her.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:54.040
Just before The Terminator hit theaters in
1984, Orion studio execs refused to screen

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.380
it for critics, showing little confidence
in it.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:01.720
The lack of love from the studio at the time
stuck with Cameron for over three decades,

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:06.120
but looking at the film now, it's impossible
to imagine how anyone could consider it a

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:06.620
failure.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.620
And thankfully, audiences at the time felt
the same way.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:14.960
The Terminator launched Cameron's career as
a director and Arnold Schwarzenegger's as

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:15.620
an actor.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:20.160
It was like nothing that had ever happened
in movies, and it proved that audiences were

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.080
willing to shell out their hard-earned money
to watch a diner waitress and her time-traveling

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.240
boyfriend get chased through the streets of
Los Angeles by a cyborg in leather.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:33.540
Cameron told the audience at the fifth annual
Hero Complex Film Festival that the fearlessness

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:37.870
it took to make The Terminator came from his
frustration in trying to break into the industry.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:38.360
He said:

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:42.440
"I was the anonymous, kind of angry, wannabe
filmmaker.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.980
There's some courage that comes from that,
you say whatever comes into your head…I

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:50.220
was kind of like a free voice in the wilderness
in that stage."

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:55.240
Terminator 2: Judgment Day not only builds
upon the world created by its predecessor,

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.080
but it's also somehow better than the original
movie.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:03.640
Over ten years after the events of The Terminator,
Sarah Connor has been institutionalized because

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.880
of her belief in time-traveling killer robots.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.840
Her son, John, lives with foster parents.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:14.300
The original T-800 has been reprogrammed as
a protector for John, and the new evil is

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:19.920
the T-1000, an updated Terminator with the
added feature of shape-shifting liquid metal.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.540
Judgment Day isn't just a continuation of
the series, it's something totally new.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:29.700
Sarah is a fighting machine, a far cry from
the scared waitress in The Terminator.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:35.820
The T-800 is no longer a threat, and this
version of the character sets up a multi-movie

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:42.000
arc for the original big bad, one that sees
an aging actor continue to reprise the role,

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.880
in spite of the fact that robots shouldn't
age.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.420
Judgment Day's T-800 was just so likable,
it didn’t matter.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.320
Plus, it gave us some fantastic catchphrases.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.940
"Hasta la vista, baby."

